    'This week, do four things. Read Proverbs 16:32 and James 1:19-20 every morning, out loud, before you open your phone. The next time someone says the Word says something, ask them, kindly, where, and read it together; that is what the Bereans did. When a conversation moves the goalposts, name the first point once, finish it, and then let it rest without a second round. And before you sleep, run the day’s hardest conversation through the Test of Philippians 4:8 and hand the person to Yahweh by name. Provenance, stated plainly: Darrell spoke this teaching into the app as a voice note and a prayer, asking why it still annoys him when the Word is misrepresented, and how Jesus and His people kept their spirit ruled. His words are rendered here for their meaning, not word for word. Every verse is quoted from the King James text this app holds.',
