      body: 'This is an invented story, told to make one point plain. Renee ran the Tuesday book circle at her library, and one evening a man named Curtis told the room, with great confidence, that the Bible says heaven helps those who help themselves. Renee felt the heat rise in her neck. She had heard it a hundred times. She opened the Word on her phone, searched, and showed him kindly that the line is not in it. Curtis frowned, then changed the subject to tithing, then to the size of the ark. Renee smiled, said once that the first point was settled, and moved the circle back to the book. She did not chase him. Two weeks later Curtis came back early, sat down beside her and said he had looked for that verse all week and could not find it. Then he asked where to start reading. Renee had not won an argument; she had kept her spirit, and the Word had done the rest. "These were more noble than those in Thessalonica, in that they received the word with all readiness of mind, and searched the scriptures daily, whether those things were so." (Acts 17:11)',
